# SCSS Mixins & Breakpoints

All responsive logic in SCSS modules flows through helpers in `src/styles/mixins.scss`, which read the `$breakpoints` map in `src/styles/settings.scss`. Never write raw `@media (min-width: …)` in component SCSS.

## The breakpoint map

```scss
// src/styles/settings.scss
$breakpoints: (
  xs: 0,
  sm: 576px,
  md: 768px,
  lg: 992px,
  xl: 1200px,
  xxl: 1400px,
);
```

Mobile-first — `xs` is the implicit default, no `@media` needed.

## How to use

```scss
@use 'mixins' as *;
```

The bare `mixins` load is resolved via `sassOptions.loadPaths: ['src/styles']` in `next.config.js`. Do not pass relative paths. Use `@use`, never the deprecated `@import`.

### `b-up($name)` — min-width (default)

```scss
.card {
  padding: 1rem;

  @include b-up(md) {
    padding: 2rem;
  }
}
```

`b-up(xs)` renders with no media wrapper (`xs = 0`).

### `b-d($name)` — max-width (rarely)

`max-width: $value - 0.02px` so it never overlaps a `b-up` at the same name. Prefer `b-up` whenever the design can be expressed mobile-first. `container.scss` uses `b-d(sm)` for the narrow gutter.

### `b-btw($lower, $upper)` — between

Inclusive on the lower end, exclusive on the upper.

### `b-o($name)` — only this step

From this breakpoint up to the next map entry. Use sparingly.

## Fluid sizing — `clamp-builder($lower, $upper, $min-size, $max-size)`

Returns a `clamp()` that scales linearly between two breakpoints. Use for long-form headings and generous container padding — not for small UI atoms.

```scss
h1 {
  font-size: clamp-builder(sm, xl, 32px, 56px);
}
```

## Hard rules

- **No raw `@media (min-width: …)` or `(max-width: …)` in component SCSS.** Always `b-up` / `b-d` / `b-btw` / `b-o`. `@media (hover: hover)` is fine.
- **No raw pixel values as mixin arguments.** Pass map names (`md`, not `768px`).
- **Default to mobile-first (`b-up`).**
- **`@use 'mixins' as *;` once per module that uses them**, and not in modules that don't.
- **Add new breakpoints to the map**, never inline a one-off. Discuss first — six steps is already plenty.
- **Sass module functions only** (`list.nth`, `map.get`, `math.div`, `meta.type-of`); stylelint rejects the global built-ins.
